# Blaze Core

Blaze Robotics Academy — Seattle-area robotics education platform: franchises, enrollments, Stripe payments, admin/coach portals, Capacitor iOS shell.

## Stack

Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind + shadcn/ui (new-york), Supabase, NextAuth v5, Stripe, Vercel AI SDK.

## Paths

Always use `@/` → `src/`. Key directories:

- `src/app/` — pages and API routes
- `src/components/ui/` — shadcn primitives (avoid casual edits)
- `src/lib/` — db, stripe, permissions, email, traffic
- `src/hooks/`, `src/contexts/`
- `v2/` — V2 database DDL scripts (schema source of truth)
- `scripts/` — migrations and manual integration tests (no Jest/Vitest)
- `_archive/` — isolated legacy code pending deletion (see `LEGACY_MANIFEST.md`)

## Global Rules

- Do not add new features under `_archive/`; check `LEGACY_MANIFEST.md` before deleting archived files

- Schema changes go in `v2/` numbered SQL files; follow `database-schema` rule for data operations
- Minimize diff scope; match patterns in the file you touch
- Do not commit `.env*` or secrets
- Do not add `*.md`, `*.sql`, or `*.pdf` to the repo (gitignored)
- Do not enable `output: 'export'` in `next.config.ts` — API routes need server runtime
- Prefer extending existing modules over new abstractions
- Run `npm run lint` after substantive changes; no automated test suite exists
- Preserve Chinese comments when editing nearby code; respond to the user in their language
